[30.123975, "o", "All files are created and verified.\r\n\r\n**`/app/jq_args.yaml`**\r\n```yaml\r\nfilter: '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}] | sort_by(.username)'\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--indent 2\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n**`/app/cmd.sh`** (the exact command executed)\r\n```sh\r\njq --indent 2 '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}] | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nImplementation notes:\r\n- `fromdateiso8601` in jq 1.6 rejects fractional seconds, so the fractional part is stripped (`sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\")`) before real ISO-8601 parsing and `strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")` formatting.\r\n- `primary_role` uses `.role"]
[30.124074, "o", "s[0] // null`, yielding JSON `null` for empty role arrays (50 such users).\r\n- `--indent 2` guarantees 2-space indentation.\r\n\r\nVerification: 346 active users out of 500; output sorted from `acosta` to `zwelch`; all dates match `YYYY-MM-DD`. Re-running through the specified `yq` + `jq` reconstruction pipeline produced a byte-identical file.\r\n"]
